{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"agent_message","text":"I fixed the problem and submitted the mitigation; the submission endpoint returned 200 (\"Submission received\"). I didn't run any end-user requests myself, so I haven't confirmed that latency is back to normal.\n\n**Cause:** the `frontend` service selected pods by the label `service-route=frontend`, and the `search` pods carried that label too. The service therefore sent part of the frontend traffic to the search pod, which listens on 8082, not 5000.\n\n**Fix:**\n- I removed the `service-route` label from the `search` deployment's pod template.\n- I changed the `frontend` service selector to `io.kompose.service=frontend`.\n\nThe `frontend` service now has one endpoint, the frontend pod on port 5000. `search` has its own endpoint on 8082 and 9092."}}
